course: dictionary
lesson: 9437
title: Stair and stairs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stair is one step. Stairs, or a staircase, is the whole set of steps that goes from one floor to another. «He ran up the stairs to bed.» Here stairs means all the steps, not just one.
explain: You can use stairs to go up or down inside a building. A flight of stairs is a set of steps between two floors. «Toad is taken up winding stairs into a grim old castle.» Winding means the stairs twist and turn as they go up.
explain: Stairs can be dangerous, so take care on them. Hold the handrail, do not run or play on the stairs, and keep them clear of toys. Look at the clue words to know which meaning the author uses: one step, or the whole set.
fact: A stair is one step; stairs, or a staircase, is the whole set of steps.
fact: Stairs go up or down between the floors of a building.
fact: «Upstairs» means on a higher floor, and «downstairs» means on a lower floor.
fact: A «flight of stairs» is a set of steps between two floors.
fact: Always hold the handrail on the stairs, and never run on them.
exercise: «He ran up the stairs to bed.» Does stairs mean one step or the whole set of steps? | *The whole set of steps | A window | A ceiling | One single step
exercise: What is the safe thing to do on stairs? | Run down them two at a time | Leave toys on them | Play a ball game on them | *Hold the handrail
exercise: What does «upstairs» mean? | *On a higher floor | On a lower floor | In the garden | Under the bed
test: «Toad is taken up winding stairs into a grim old castle.» What does winding describe? | *Twisting and turning | Very fast | Wet and slippery | Made of gold
test: What do we call the whole set of steps from one floor to another? | A doorway | A stair | *A staircase | A handrail
exam: Which word is correct? «One ___ is a single step, and the whole set of steps is called stairs.» | *stair | floor | staircase | handrail
